{
 "note": "APPEND-ONLY successor. ARM-2 round-26 CORRECTIONS (Codex): all six findings executed, VERIFIED AGAINST A REAL MEDZEN CLOUDTRAIL EVENT + LIVE IAM SIMULATION before writing the fixes. CRITICAL-1 (CloudTrail lookup found nothing): confirmed a real CreateTrainingJob event has an EMPTY Resources list, so round-25's ResourceName lookup returned zero \u2014 a genuine job would fail authoritative verification. fetch_creation_event now queries by EventName=CreateTrainingJob within the receipt's CreationTime window (+/-30min), decodes each event, filters by requestParameters.trainingJobName, and keeps only the SUCCESSFUL one (errorCode absent \u2014 a failed-then-retried create cannot supply a stale record); exactly one required. CRITICAL-2 (comparison rejected real, accepted incomplete): the real event carries service-added defaults the render never sent \u2014 disableEFA=false, withWarmPoolValidationError=false, trainingJobArn=<arn> (top-level) and enableSageMakerMetricsTimeSeries=false (nested in algorithmSpecification), useReservedCapacity=false (nested in resourceConfig) \u2014 which round-25 REJECTED, while a record with only a correct trainingJobName PASSED. verify_creation_request_parameters is now TWO-SIDED: every RENDERED field must be present+equal, and the ONLY tolerated extras are the empirically-observed inert defaults (all False; trainingJobArn bound to the receipt ARN). NEW verify_creation_event checks the ENVELOPE (eventSource/name, awsRegion, recipientAccountId, no error, responseElements.trainingJobArn, and the sessionIssuer PRINCIPAL bound to the calibration role) so it proves WHICH role launched the job. A sanitized REAL event is committed as a fixture and a test asserts its service-added shape is exactly what the comparator tolerates. HIGH-3 (preprocessing): _preprocess_wave now uses F.layer_norm(wave, wave.shape, eps=1e-5) \u2014 POPULATION variance, matching Meta's pinned audio.py exactly \u2014 not sample variance (wave.var() drifted ~1.4e-4 on 16k samples, more on short inputs); torch test asserts allclose to F.layer_norm. MEDIUM-4 (parity receipt weak): verify_calibration now requires the EXACT upstream pipeline id (CANONICAL_UPSTREAM_PIPELINE) and canonical scorer (not a substring), and the parity receipt binds each checked row's audio_checksum_sha256 + hyp_sha256, cross-checked as a subset of the scored dev rows; the wrapper records them. MEDIUM-5 (disk preflight): required_free_bytes = declared archive + ARCHIVE_MAX_AGGREGATE_BYTES + margin (extracted bytes are NOT bounded by the compressed size); test proves it exceeds the old archive*2. MEDIUM-6 (calibration role doc-only): NEW infra/arm2_calibration_role.tf + platform/iam/medzen-arm2-calibration-role.json create medzen-arm2-calibration-role \u2014 CreateTrainingJob ONLY for medzen-b5-b5-universal-arm2-ftcal-2026-001, tag calibration, the same hard conditions (g6.xlarge/subnet/SG/KMS/runtime<=7200), the NoRemoteDebugEver deny, exact artifact read (research/b5-training/b5-universal-arm2-ftcal-2026-001/output/*), trainer-role PassRole \u2014 trust bound to the owner-approved arm2-calibration environment + the reusable arm2-calibration-launch-exec.yml (caller arm2-calibration-launch.yml, confirm_launch=LAUNCH gate). LIVE-SIMULATED via iam simulate-custom-policy: allowed (calibration job), explicitDeny (remote debug), implicitDeny (arm-1 job), implicitDeny (tier=arm). The role is enabled in terraform.tfvars alongside the publisher; the saved plan is now 4 add (publisher role+policy, calibration role+policy) / 1 change (arm-launch deny) / 0 destroy (sha 82106b3e...). Suites: 146 calibration host tests; 185 with torch; CI-matching no-torch 2424 passed / 0 failed. HOLDS UNCHANGED: NO Arm-2 compute, sealed data, promotion or deployment; publisher + calibration roles undeployed (dark) pending the final review + owner activation.",
